PART E -- BREACH, PENALTIES, AND TERMINATION
==============================================================================

E1. Breach includes: using locked features without payment, copying or
    redistributing the Software, removing copyright notices, attacking
    the service, or violating any term herein.

E2. Penalties:
    - No legal acceptance: access blocked.
    - Unpaid package use: access refused, logged, and debt equal to the
      package price.
    - Chargeback after use: immediate relock + package price + provider fees.
    - Copying, reselling, or stripping copyright: immediate termination
      + damages not less than K 500 plus proven losses and costs.
    - Attack, fraud, or abuse: permanent ban and report to host and
      authorities.

E3. Termination: The licence ends immediately upon material breach,
    including copying the Software, bypassing locks, attacking the
    service, or refusing the current legal version. Upon termination
    you must stop all use. Your business data exports remain available
    to you. No refund is issued for breach.

E4. Enforcement: Ephraim Zulu and KAZE Traders will pursue all available
    remedies, including civil action, criminal charges where applicable,
    and prosecution of anyone who violates this licence or the Terms of
    Service.

